    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" caput="4" para="true">LIBER</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1" caput="4">QVARTVS</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="1" caput="4">PHYSICORVM</l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De motu Generationis.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">OMnis alteratio fit in gratiam</l>
    <l n="6">generationis. Non enim sa-</l>
    <l n="7">tis est naturali agenti praepa-</l>
    <l n="8">rare subiectum alterando, &amp;</l>
    <l n="9">disponendo; sed praeterea</l>
    <l n="10">mouet se se ad mixti substan-</l>
    <l n="11">tialis generationem. Idcirco exigit doctri-</l>
    <l n="12">næ ordo, vt postquam egimus de altera-</l>
    <l n="13">tione, alium aggrediamur motum, qui</l>
    <l n="14">dicitur generationis. Quia vero gene-</l>
    <l n="15">rationem vnius consequitur ex commu-</l>
    <l n="16">ni axiomate corruptio alterius, hoc etiam</l>
    <l n="17">libro materiam de corruptione amplecti-</l>
    <l n="18">mur, totam doctrinam de ortu, &amp; interi-</l>
    <l n="19">tu, qnæ alibi traditur à Philosophis, huc</l>
    <l n="20">opportunius, ni fallor, translaturi. Qua-</l>
    <l n="21">druplici autem disputatione rem totam</l>
    <l n="22">expediemus. Prima erit de generatione,</l>
    <l n="23">an &amp; quid sit. Secunda, quomodo</l>
    <l n="24">illa exerceatur. Tertia de cor-</l>
    <l n="25">ruptione, an &amp; quid sit.</l>
    <l n="26">Quarta, quomodo</l>
    <l n="27">ea contin-</l>
    <l n="28">gat.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The initial "O" is a large woodcut initial. Text reads "Omnis" with the O decorative; transcribed as O joined to "Mnis" (OMnis). The "qnæ" spelling is as printed. Page number 305 is printed at top right.</notes>
